WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:02.760
Local does not automatically mean secure.

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:06.800
A model server bound to the wrong network interface, an unauthenticated API,

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.090
a shared desktop session,

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:12.085
or an exposed web interface can make sensitive prompts and compute available to

00:00:12.085 --> 00:00:13.360
unauthorized users.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.200
Apply least privilege, individual accounts, authentication, network segmentation,

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:21.540
secure remote access, request limits, and administrative logging according to risk.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:25.278
Do not expose a local inference service directly to untrusted networks.

00:00:25.278 --> 00:00:27.690
Handle model downloads as supply-chain inputs.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.415
Use trusted sources, review licenses and provenance,

00:00:30.415 --> 00:00:33.540
validate expected files where appropriate, scan supporting code,

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.920
and avoid running unknown installers or model-specific scripts without review.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.220
Prompts, retrieved documents, outputs, uploads, caches, chat histories, telemetry,

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:44.240
and logs may contain sensitive data.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.635
Define collection, access, redaction, retention, backup, and deletion.

00:00:48.635 --> 00:00:51.440
Disable unnecessary logging rather than assuming it is harmless.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.950
Patch the operating system, drivers, runtimes, interfaces, libraries,

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:57.528
and integration code through a tested process.

00:00:57.528 --> 00:01:01.780
Back up configuration, prompts or evaluation assets where required, access controls,

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:03.440
and service documentation.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:07.860
Models themselves may be reproducible downloads, but local customizations may not be.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:11.720
Monitor availability, latency, memory errors, queue depth, temperature, disk,

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:14.515
failed requests, and unauthorized use.

00:01:14.515 --> 00:01:17.730
Responsible operation also requires model evaluation, user guidance,

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:19.220
escalation for harmful output,

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:22.600
and a clear decision about when a cloud or human expert is more appropriate.
